# Cloudflare Pages headers — docs.nullrun.io
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file is consumed by Cloudflare Pages when the site is served from
# there. Until DNS is cut over from `nullrunio.github.io` to the
# Cloudflare Pages project, this file is dormant — GitHub Pages serves
# `site/` directly without honoring `_headers`.
#
# MkDocs copies this file verbatim into `site/_headers` at build time
# (it's a static asset, not a markdown page). The Cloudflare Pages
# GitHub Action in `.github/workflows/pages-cf.yml` then deploys `site/`
# as the publish directory.
#
# Mozilla Observatory credit map (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/observatory):
#   • content-security-policy          → CSP test (header form)
#   • strict-transport-security        → HSTS test
#   • x-content-type-options           → X-Content-Type-Options test
#   • x-frame-options                  → X-Frame-Options test
#                                          (frame-ancestors in CSP also
#                                          accepted; both set for belt
#                                          + suspenders on legacy UAs)
#   • referrer-policy                  → Referrer-Policy test
#   • permissions-policy               → Permissions-Policy test
#   • cross-origin-opener-policy       → COOP test
#   • cross-origin-resource-policy     → CORP test
# Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy is intentionally omitted — `require-corp`
# breaks cross-origin font loads from fonts.gstatic.com, and a docs
# site doesn't need cross-origin isolation for SharedArrayBuffer.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval'; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self' https://github.com; base-uri 'self'

# Print edition at /print/ — relaxed CSP because the inline print-button
# handler and inline anchors don't fit the default-src 'self' baseline
# cleanly across older browsers. HSTS / X-CTO / X-Frame still apply.
/print/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'
